; The instrumentation backend is named here, and this library is the one where
; naming it looks like a mistake. It is not. A backend is absent until
; [--instrument-with assay] asks for it, and the runtime it links comes from
; assay's own [ppx_runtime_libraries] rather than from the field below. So the
; [lingo_runtime] a generated parser links carries nothing of assay's, and the
; opam package gains no dependency either.

(library
 (name lingo_runtime)
 (public_name lingo_runtime)
 (libraries ir siesta handsome)
 (instrumentation
  (backend assay)))
